      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "BCR-ABL inhibition made targeted molecular therapy a clinically persuasive paradigm and transformed chronic myeloid leukemia outcomes.",
        "attribution": "Lydon contributed critically to inhibitor development, Druker to clinical translation, and Sawyers to mechanistic and resistance-focused validation.",
        "maturity": "The causal target, clinical benefit, and broader influence on cancer medicine have been established over decades.",
